cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Faultiva in your work, please cite it using these metadata.
title: >-
  Faultiva: Hybrid Fault Detection and Localization for VLSI Circuits
abstract: >-
  A self-contained tool for diagnosing single stuck-at faults in gate-level VLSI
  circuits from observed output alone. Detection and localization use exact
  behaviour-signature retrieval with zero learned parameters, backed by a
  dictionary of 127,484 signature-to-site entries across four characterized
  circuits. A third stage verifies each candidate with a 93,185-parameter
  multilayer perceptron over 646 structural features at a locked threshold of
  0.4965. The behavioural and structural stages use disjoint evidence, so
  agreement between them is corroboration rather than self-confirmation. End to
  end inference takes roughly 0.5 milliseconds on a single CPU core. Measured
  across 7,849,696 transactions with zero false alarms; exact-site localization
  reaches 0.4516 on SHA-256 and 0.3675 on AES. Localization returns fault
  equivalence classes rather than always a single site, because 83 to 99 percent
  of ambiguous candidate sets are structurally indistinguishable from any
  response-based method.
